Language: en

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:24.550 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  so  brenda and i had a common vision of  raising our children in a house like  this  when we were design students  [Music]  we intentionally looked for a house with  a basement so that we could turn it into  a quiet  private workspace that was separated  from family life upstairs  [Music]  moving here was a deliberate attempt to  escape from the city area which i grew  up in  and be with nature in hope that the  hermetic environment  would allow for more reflection when i  first started age 55 more than 20 years  ago  i asked myself what is a workspace  why do people work in offices can we  redefine a workspace  and can they be mobile and would the  workspace  influence the type of work produced  it soon became obvious that ultimately  my mind is the design studio  the design studio is there for anywhere  and everywhere  it is an inner world that travels with  me wherever i go  in search of ideas  [Music]  the act of walking seeing and thinking  makes me feel alive  spotting the unfamiliar within the  familiar intrigues me  i'm fascinated by nature because nature  is the empty thesis of design which is  nurtured and man-made  yet nature has its own universal design  which can inform the way we create  the lower piers trail allows me to be  conveniently immersed in nature and  observe its wonders  [Music]  the trio's thoughtfully designed  boardwalk integrates harmoniously with  the surrounding greens and allows for a  safe and pleasant stroll  the signages along the boardwalk provide  clear information  and are unintrusive  we don't have to visit a museum to  appreciate good design  because design is everywhere often it is  at the older strata titled shopping  centers where design  gems and unexpected oddities can be  found  these independently owned shops are  refreshingly authentic as compared to  the glossy stores which mostly occupy  our retail landscape  one of these shops is memory lane at the  adelphi  which carries a wide range of selected  records  like a mini graphic design museum some  of the most famous works can be found  here  from iconic album covers designed by  peter saville and mark farrow  to the surreal imagery created by  hypnosis for pink floyd and black  sabbath  i admire artists who have the indie or  independent spirit  those who dare experiment and stay true  to their artistic expression  while bravely ignoring what is radio  friendly and acceptable by society  these bans have shown me that sticking  to one's belief and passion can lead to  unexpected possibilities  skateboard culture is one of the  influences behind streetwear which in  turn has a big influence on fashion  today  speed fire at peninsular shopping center  is a treasure trove of  original skateboard graphics and  illustrations  brands like santa cruz oil peralta and  independent trucks have been around for  decades and continue to provide a whole  array of sought after merchandise  what makes the graphics cool is that  they are not just merely a part of the  spot  but the association with a subculture of  free spirited risk takers  who embrace failure as part of their  creative pursuit  [Music]  the extreme skatepark is a fascinating  urban landscape and piece of  architecture  parts of it reminiscent of brutally  sculptures  consisting of a vertical and combo bowl  as well as a mix  of street obstacles this control  environment is a far cry from the days  when skateboarding stunts were practiced  illegally  in public spaces often causing vandalism  and public disruption  but perhaps this is one of the things  that makes skateboard subculture  inspiring  skateboard culture is about being  disruptive and breaking the rules of  established norms and by doing so new  movements and audiences  emerge  subcultures have played a big role in  shaping the way many of us see  things through its lens we definitely  can learn to be more open  and inclusive towards alternative forms  of expression  opinions thinking and ways of living  my name is hansen ho i'm a graphic  designer at age 55  do i continue reading  you

